NNAAMMEE
     wwccttoommbb — convert a wide-character code to a character

LLIIBBRRAARRYY
     Standard C Library (libc, -lc)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ##iinncclluuddee <<ssttddlliibb..hh>>

     _i_n_t
     wwccttoommbb(_c_h_a_r _*_m_b_c_h_a_r, _w_c_h_a_r___t _w_c_h_a_r);

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The wwccttoommbb() function converts a wide character _w_c_h_a_r into a multibyte
     character and stores the result in _m_b_c_h_a_r.  The object pointed to by
     _m_b_c_h_a_r must be large enough to accommodate the multibyte character, which
     may be up to MB_LEN_MAX bytes.

     A call with a null _m_b_c_h_a_r pointer returns nonzero if the current locale
     requires shift states, zero otherwise; if shift states are required, the
     shift state is reset to the initial state.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If _m_b_c_h_a_r is NULL, the wwccttoommbb() function returns nonzero if shift states
     are supported, zero otherwise.  If _m_b_c_h_a_r is valid, wwccttoommbb() returns the
     number of bytes processed in _m_b_c_h_a_r, or -1 if no multibyte character
     could be recognized or converted.  In this case, wwccttoommbb()'s internal con‐
     version state is undefined.

EERRRROORRSS
     The wwccttoommbb() function will fail if:

     [EILSEQ]           An invalid multibyte sequence was detected.

     [EINVAL]           The internal conversion state is invalid.

